# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - this patch has been disabled.
#
# The Virtualization.framework (colima/lima VM) patch that used to live here has
# been moved to:
#
#   @anthropic-ai+sandbox-runtime+0.0.77+002+virtualization.patch.disabled
#
# It was disabled because granting a sandboxed agent access to a VM is a
# sandbox-escape vector: the guest does not honor our denyRead/denyWrite, so a
# mounted $HOME (which colima mounts by default) is readable and writable from
# inside the VM, and `docker run -v /:/host` reaches anything the VM can see.
# See vz-problems.md for the full analysis.
#
# This file is left in place, empty, rather than deleted, so that the numbering
# is not silently reused and so anyone looking for patch 002 finds this note.
# patch-package tolerates a patch with no hunks.
#
# To re-enable, see the instructions in the .disabled file.
